Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.96,0:00:22.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,今天的《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:00:20.96,0:00:22.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Today on How It's Made,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.04,0:00:27.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮划艇，为所有人心中的冒险家打造
Dialogue: 1,0:00:25.04,0:00:27.60,Original,,0,0,0,,kayaks made for the adventurer in us all.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.56,0:00:34.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,安全靴，建筑工地上硬汉的最佳伙伴
Dialogue: 1,0:00:30.56,0:00:34.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Safety boots, a hard man's best friend on the building site.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.64,0:00:39.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,电子招牌，来自天空的信息
Dialogue: 1,0:00:36.64,0:00:39.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Electronic signs, messages from the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.84,0:00:44.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有麦片，为大众烹制早餐
Dialogue: 1,0:00:41.84,0:00:44.56,Original,,0,0,0,,And cereals, making breakfast for the masses.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.36,0:00:45.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,但首先
Dialogue: 1,0:00:45.36,0:00:45.92,Original,,0,0,0,,But first,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.64,0:00:52.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,过去，皮划艇由木头和皮革制成
Dialogue: 1,0:00:48.64,0:00:52.08,Original,,0,0,0,,in days gone by, kayaks were made of wood and animal skin,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.32,0:00:54.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,是狩猎采集者赖以求生的工具
Dialogue: 1,0:00:52.32,0:00:54.40,Original,,0,0,0,,and used by hunter gatherers to survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.68,0:00:59.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,再看今天，皮划艇的形象焕然一新
Dialogue: 1,0:00:55.68,0:00:59.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Fast forward to today, and kayaks have updated their image.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.08,0:01:02.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,如今它们是塑料制品的杰作
Dialogue: 1,0:01:00.08,0:01:02.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Now they're marvels of molded plastic,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.56,0:01:05.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,令各地运动爱好者趋之若鹜
Dialogue: 1,0:01:02.56,0:01:05.28,Original,,0,0,0,,coveted by sports enthusiasts far and wide.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.88,0:01:14.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮划艇由塑料在镍制模具上熔化成型
Dialogue: 1,0:01:10.88,0:01:14.88,Original,,0,0,0,,A kayak is formed by the melting of plastic on a mould of nickel.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.76,0:01:19.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,模具由上下两半组成
Dialogue: 1,0:01:15.76,0:01:19.84,Original,,0,0,0,,This mould is made in two parts, an upper and a lower section.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.36,0:01:24.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,模具表面光滑无比
Dialogue: 1,0:01:21.36,0:01:24.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The surface of the mould is perfectly smooth,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.32,0:01:27.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,镜面抛光确保出色的光泽
Dialogue: 1,0:01:24.32,0:01:27.28,Original,,0,0,0,,and has a mirror finish that guarantees an excellent luster.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.40,0:01:35.42,Translation,,0,0,0,,图案在成型前铺在模具上
Dialogue: 1,0:01:32.40,0:01:35.42,Original,,0,0,0,,The graphics are laid on the mould before moulding begins
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.78,0:01:38.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,成型时便会印入塑料之中
Dialogue: 1,0:01:35.78,0:01:38.40,Original,,0,0,0,,so that they become impregnated into the plastic.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.60,0:01:44.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,这需要稳健的双手，因为贴纸一旦贴错位置便无法揭起
Dialogue: 1,0:01:39.60,0:01:44.32,Original,,0,0,0,,It takes a steady hand because these stickers can't be lifted off if they've been badly positioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.56,0:01:53.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,这就是用来熔化成型船体的线型低密度聚乙烯
Dialogue: 1,0:01:50.56,0:01:53.76,Original,,0,0,0,,This is the linear polyethylene which will be melted to form the shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.64,0:01:59.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,聚乙烯有几种颜色，粉末用量取决于要造的皮划艇型号
Dialogue: 1,0:01:54.64,0:01:59.92,Original,,0,0,0,,It comes in several colours, and the amount of powder used is determined by the kayak model to be made.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.08,0:02:07.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮划艇的其他部件，比如储物舱盖
Dialogue: 1,0:02:04.08,0:02:07.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Other parts of the kayak, such as the baggage compartment cover,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.00,0:02:11.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,中央支撑和座椅等，则在各自的模具中成型
Dialogue: 1,0:02:08.00,0:02:11.68,Original,,0,0,0,,the central support, and seats, are created in separate moulds.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.36,0:02:34.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,进窑前用夹具把模具牢牢夹紧，避免聚乙烯流失
Dialogue: 1,0:02:29.36,0:02:34.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Before entering the oven, the moulds are securely closed with clamps to avoid any loss of polythene.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.68,0:02:42.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮划艇模具被放到输送车上，对准窑口
Dialogue: 1,0:02:38.68,0:02:42.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The kayak mould is put onto a transporter and placed facing the oven.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.64,0:02:50.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,由于船体尺寸很大，这座窑炉是专门定制的
Dialogue: 1,0:02:46.64,0:02:50.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Because of the large dimensions of the craft, the oven had to be custom made.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.20,0:02:54.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,它长7米，直径1.7米
Dialogue: 1,0:02:51.20,0:02:54.72,Original,,0,0,0,,It's 7 metres long with a diameter of 1.7 metres.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.44,0:02:59.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,聚乙烯在288摄氏度熔化
Dialogue: 1,0:02:55.44,0:02:59.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The polythene melts at 288 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.36,0:03:14.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,为了让粉末均匀布满整个模具，模具会沿多个轴转动
Dialogue: 1,0:03:09.36,0:03:14.08,Original,,0,0,0,,To completely distribute the powder throughout the mould, it pivots on several axes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.96,0:03:17.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,它自身旋转，窑炉来回摆动
Dialogue: 1,0:03:14.96,0:03:17.76,Original,,0,0,0,,It turns on itself while the oven oscillates
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.84,0:03:19.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,向前后各摆动30度
Dialogue: 1,0:03:17.84,0:03:19.92,Original,,0,0,0,,30 degrees towards the front and rear.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.64,0:03:22.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,这种工艺叫作滚塑
Dialogue: 1,0:03:20.64,0:03:22.96,Original,,0,0,0,,This procedure is termed rock and roll.
Dialogue: 2,0:03:20.64,0:03:25.14,Annotation,,0,0,0,,滚塑工艺：模具旋转摇摆使粉末均匀贴壁
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.72,0:03:30.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,20分钟后，加热完成，模具出炉
Dialogue: 1,0:03:26.72,0:03:30.64,Original,,0,0,0,,After 20 minutes, the cooking is complete and the mould exits the oven.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.36,0:03:34.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,但塑料需要冷却才能凝固
Dialogue: 1,0:03:31.36,0:03:34.00,Original,,0,0,0,,But the plastic has to cool in order to solidify.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.36,0:03:40.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,为此，他们把模具放进冷却室
Dialogue: 1,0:03:37.36,0:03:40.40,Original,,0,0,0,,To do this, they place the mould in this cooling chamber.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.96,0:03:43.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,冷却不能太快，否则会变形
Dialogue: 1,0:03:40.96,0:03:43.92,Original,,0,0,0,,It must not be cooled too quickly, or it becomes deformed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.80,0:03:49.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,一艘4.8米的皮划艇长度可收缩达15厘米
Dialogue: 1,0:03:44.80,0:03:49.20,Original,,0,0,0,,A 4.8 metre kayak can lose up to 15 centimetres of its length.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.56,0:03:57.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,模具上盖终于被揭开
Dialogue: 1,0:03:54.56,0:03:57.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The cover of the mould is at last lifted off.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.16,0:04:09.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,较小的模具也同样脱模
Dialogue: 1,0:04:08.16,0:04:09.36,Original,,0,0,0,,As are the smaller moulds.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.28,0:04:19.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来，皮划艇进入机械加工环节
Dialogue: 1,0:04:17.28,0:04:19.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Next, the kayak can proceed to the machining.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.36,0:04:34.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,模具两半接缝处留下的塑料毛边被清理干净
Dialogue: 1,0:04:29.36,0:04:34.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Any plastic ridges left by the joint between the two halves of the mould are removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.28,0:04:37.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮划艇随后进入精加工车间
Dialogue: 1,0:04:35.28,0:04:37.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The kayak now moves to the finishing department.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.56,0:04:40.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先是拧上提手
Dialogue: 1,0:04:38.56,0:04:40.96,Original,,0,0,0,,This begins with the screwing on of the carrying handles.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.20,0:04:45.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,储物舱的开口被裁出
Dialogue: 1,0:04:43.20,0:04:45.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The opening for the baggage compartment is cut,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.08,0:04:49.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,同时安装镶边
Dialogue: 1,0:04:48.08,0:04:49.76,Original,,0,0,0,,and the trimming is also installed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.12,0:04:59.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,中央支撑就位
Dialogue: 1,0:04:58.12,0:04:59.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The central support is positioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.32,0:05:04.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,它起着重要作用，连接船体的底部和顶部
Dialogue: 1,0:05:00.32,0:05:04.24,Original,,0,0,0,,It plays an important role because it links the bottom and top portions of the craft.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.36,0:05:12.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来只需完成储物舱的最后安装
Dialogue: 1,0:05:09.36,0:05:12.56,Original,,0,0,0,,All that remains to be done now is to finish the baggage compartment.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.36,0:05:17.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,装好固定件，盖上舱盖，用固定带压紧
Dialogue: 1,0:05:13.36,0:05:17.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Fasteners are attached, then the cover is put in place and held down with a retaining strap.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.52,0:05:29.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后，皮划艇打包发货
Dialogue: 1,0:05:27.52,0:05:29.84,Original,,0,0,0,,Finally, the kayak is packaged for delivery.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.64,0:05:32.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,冒险之旅即将开启
Dialogue: 1,0:05:30.64,0:05:32.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The adventure is ready to begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.84,0:05:46.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,这个教训，希望你不必用惨痛的经历去领会
Dialogue: 1,0:05:43.84,0:05:46.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Here's a lesson we hope you won't have to learn the hard way.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.68,0:05:51.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,干活时锤子掉下来，你的脚趾可能就要遭殃了
Dialogue: 1,0:05:47.68,0:05:51.84,Original,,0,0,0,,Drop a hammer on the job, and you might have a few broken toes to show for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.96,0:05:54.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,这时就该坚固的安全靴登场了
Dialogue: 1,0:05:52.96,0:05:54.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Enter the sturdy work boot.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.60,0:05:58.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,穿上这样一双靴子，你的双脚就有望安然无恙
Dialogue: 1,0:05:55.60,0:05:58.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Lace on a pair, and the chances are your feet will survive
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.40,0:06:00.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,即便在最危险的建筑工地
Dialogue: 1,0:05:58.40,0:06:00.64,Original,,0,0,0,,even the most hazardous of building sites.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.80,0:06:06.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,安全靴由皮革制成
Dialogue: 1,0:06:04.80,0:06:06.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Work boots are made from leather,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.48,0:06:09.14,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮革经过鞣制和防水处理
Dialogue: 1,0:06:06.48,0:06:09.14,Original,,0,0,0,,which undergoes a tanning and waterproofing treatment.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.88,0:06:12.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮革被送入削匀机
Dialogue: 1,0:06:10.88,0:06:12.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The hide is put through a shaver.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.04,0:06:16.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,削匀机使皮革厚薄均匀、张开毛孔，以便进一步处理
Dialogue: 1,0:06:13.04,0:06:16.80,Original,,0,0,0,,It evens up the leather and opens its pores before it receives further treatment.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.24,0:06:29.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后皮革被重新放回复鞣转鼓
Dialogue: 1,0:06:26.24,0:06:29.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The hides are then put back into the retanning drum,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.44,0:06:34.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,水、着色剂以及复鞣溶液，在转鼓中处理皮革
Dialogue: 1,0:06:29.44,0:06:34.40,Original,,0,0,0,,where water, colouring products, as well as the retanning solutions treat the hides
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.48,0:06:37.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,温度在32到60摄氏度之间
Dialogue: 1,0:06:34.48,0:06:37.84,Original,,0,0,0,,at temperatures between 32 and 60 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.00,0:06:45.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,取出皮革，加热到70摄氏度, 真空干燥2分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:06:40.00,0:06:45.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The hides are removed, and the leather vacuum dried for 2 minutes at a temperature of 70 degrees.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.32,0:06:48.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后皮革需要挂晾24到48小时
Dialogue: 1,0:06:46.32,0:06:48.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the hide will be hung for 24 to 48 hours.
Dialogue: 1,0:06:53.42,0:06:56.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The hides are then stretched on a vacuum drying plate
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.42,0:06:56.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮革随后被平铺在真空干燥板上拉伸
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.88,0:06:58.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,去除所有褶皱
Dialogue: 1,0:06:56.88,0:06:58.96,Original,,0,0,0,,and evened out to get rid of any creases.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.16,0:07:11.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些皮料将近2平方米，制作一只靴子大约需要0.4平方米
Dialogue: 1,0:07:04.16,0:07:11.68,Original,,0,0,0,,These pieces of leather measure almost 2 square metres, with 0.4 square metres needed to make a boot.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.16,0:07:13.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在可以开始裁切了
Dialogue: 1,0:07:12.16,0:07:13.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the cutting can begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.48,0:07:16.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,冲裁模借助压力机
Dialogue: 1,0:07:14.48,0:07:16.00,Original,,0,0,0,,This punch, with the help of a press,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.48,0:07:17.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,裁出不同形状的皮革片
Dialogue: 1,0:07:16.48,0:07:17.92,Original,,0,0,0,,cuts the different pieces of leather.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.32,0:07:24.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,他们还裁切棕色布片
Dialogue: 1,0:07:22.32,0:07:24.48,Original,,0,0,0,,They also cut brown fabric pieces,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.80,0:07:29.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是靴子的内衬，由泡沫基材和编织涤纶纤维制成
Dialogue: 1,0:07:24.80,0:07:29.52,Original,,0,0,0,,the interior lining of the boot, made from a foam base and woven polyester fibres.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.64,0:07:35.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,片皮机在缝制前把边缘削薄
Dialogue: 1,0:07:32.64,0:07:35.36,Original,,0,0,0,,This paring machine thins the edges before they are sewn.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.12,0:07:46.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,裁切时，每块皮革都会按尺寸分类标识
Dialogue: 1,0:07:39.12,0:07:46.40,Original,,0,0,0,,During the cutting, each piece of leather is identified by its size.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.96,0:07:48.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在开始组装靴子
Dialogue: 1,0:07:46.96,0:07:48.72,Original,,0,0,0,,They now begin to assemble the boot.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.36,0:07:51.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,两侧缝合在一起
Dialogue: 1,0:07:49.36,0:07:51.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The two sides are sewn together.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.96,0:07:58.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在开始组装靴头
Dialogue: 1,0:07:56.96,0:07:58.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the front of the boot is assembled.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.28,0:08:01.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,多余的皮革被逐步裁掉
Dialogue: 1,0:07:59.28,0:08:01.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Excess leather is progressively cut away.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.00,0:08:08.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来安装钢、黄铜或铝制的鞋眼
Dialogue: 1,0:08:04.00,0:08:08.08,Original,,0,0,0,,The eyelets, made of steel, brass or aluminium, are then positioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.16,0:08:13.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里他们用鞋钉把足模固定在鞋楦上
Dialogue: 1,0:08:10.16,0:08:13.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Here they attach a foot mount on a form with tacks.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.30,0:08:22.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,把鞋楦放入靴内，以便组装靴头
Dialogue: 1,0:08:17.30,0:08:22.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The last or mount is placed in the boot to facilitate the assembly of the front part.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.32,0:08:30.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,起绒机在内衬上除去不平整之处，然后进入下一步
Dialogue: 1,0:08:24.32,0:08:30.00,Original,,0,0,0,,This carding machine removes any unevenness at the level of the lining before proceeding to the next step.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.32,0:08:34.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在安装淬火钢包头
Dialogue: 1,0:08:32.32,0:08:34.56,Original,,0,0,0,,They now install the tempered steel toe cap.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:32.32,0:08:35.32,Annotation,,0,0,0,,淬火钢包头：防砸保护钢片
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.32,0:08:38.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,拉紧内衬，装入并固定包头
Dialogue: 1,0:08:35.32,0:08:38.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The lining is pulled and the cap inserted and fixed in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.80,0:08:46.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,皮革被翻折到靴底下方
Dialogue: 1,0:08:44.80,0:08:46.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The leather is folded beneath the boot.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.52,0:08:53.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,底部用鞋钉固定，两侧则用热熔胶在绷帮机上粘合
Dialogue: 1,0:08:47.52,0:08:53.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The bottom secured with a tack and the sides fastened with hot glue on this seam and side lasting machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.32,0:08:56.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,靴头至此完成
Dialogue: 1,0:08:54.32,0:08:56.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The boot front is now finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.90,0:09:11.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,此时取下先前安装的鞋楦
Dialogue: 1,0:09:07.90,0:09:11.44,Original,,0,0,0,,At this stage, the mould installed earlier on is removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.78,0:09:18.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在安装鞋底
Dialogue: 1,0:09:16.78,0:09:18.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the sole is installed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.96,0:09:22.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,后跟芯由松木制成，固定在鞋底上
Dialogue: 1,0:09:18.96,0:09:22.48,Original,,0,0,0,,The heel core is made of pine and secured onto the sole.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.64,0:09:30.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里他们加工并融接靴头的橡胶鞋底
Dialogue: 1,0:09:26.64,0:09:30.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Here they proceed with machining and welding the rubber sole of the boot tip.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.28,0:09:36.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,这叫硫化，在165摄氏度下进行
Dialogue: 1,0:09:31.28,0:09:36.16,Original,,0,0,0,,It's called vulcanisation, done at a temperature of 165 degrees,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.20,0:09:39.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,鞋底被牢固地装上
Dialogue: 1,0:09:37.20,0:09:39.36,Original,,0,0,0,,and the sole is solidly installed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.24,0:09:46.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器打磨鞋底边缘，去除硫化残留
Dialogue: 1,0:09:42.24,0:09:46.64,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine sands the edges of the sole to eliminate any vulcanisation residue.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.44,0:09:48.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后涂上密封剂
Dialogue: 1,0:09:47.44,0:09:48.80,Original,,0,0,0,,A sealant is then applied.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.60,0:09:54.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在把内底放入靴内
Dialogue: 1,0:09:51.60,0:09:54.08,Original,,0,0,0,,They now place an inner sole inside the boot.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.82,0:10:00.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后的工序是穿鞋带和缝制标签
Dialogue: 1,0:09:56.82,0:10:00.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The finishing touches are the laces and stitching of the labels.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.82,0:10:09.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,靴子随即送往包装区
Dialogue: 1,0:10:06.82,0:10:09.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The boots now leave for the packaging area.
Dialogue: 1,0:10:12.24,0:10:19.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Building a pair of boots required no less than 123 different fabrication steps, including packaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.26,0:10:19.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,加上包装， 制作一双靴子至少需要123道不同的制造工序
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.76,0:10:28.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,每双靴子需要101米尼龙、棉线和涤纶线，以及近1平方米厚实耐磨的皮革
Dialogue: 1,0:10:19.76,0:10:28.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Each pair needs 101 metres of nylon, cotton and polyester threads, and close to a square metre of thick and rugged leather.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.88,0:10:30.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,不过你的双脚值得如此
Dialogue: 1,0:10:28.88,0:10:30.72,Original,,0,0,0,,But your feet are worth it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.04,0:10:37.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来请看《造物小百科》：电子招牌
Dialogue: 1,0:10:33.04,0:10:37.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Coming up in how it's made: electronic signs.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.08,0:10:40.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,霓虹灯和点阵广告的时代已经过去
Dialogue: 1,0:10:38.08,0:10:40.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Gone are the days of neon and dot matrix Advertising.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.44,0:10:43.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,信息传递得无比清晰
Dialogue: 1,0:10:41.44,0:10:43.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The message is coming through crystal clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.32,0:10:48.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有麦片，大众的早餐
Dialogue: 1,0:10:46.32,0:10:48.72,Original,,0,0,0,,And cereal, breakfast for the masses,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.36,0:10:52.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,机器打造出甜蜜的清晨盛宴
Dialogue: 1,0:10:49.36,0:10:52.88,Original,,0,0,0,,as the machines create a sweet early morning feast.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.04,0:11:06.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎回到《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:11:05.04,0:11:06.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome back to how it's made.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.08,0:11:11.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,稍后我们看看麦片，大众的早餐
Dialogue: 1,0:11:08.08,0:11:11.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Later, we look at cereal, breakfast for the masses,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.60,0:11:13.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,机器们各就各位大显身手
Dialogue: 1,0:11:11.60,0:11:13.20,Original,,0,0,0,,as the machines get down to business.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.32,0:11:14.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,但首先
Dialogue: 1,0:11:14.32,0:11:14.88,Original,,0,0,0,,But first,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.12,0:11:19.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,在东京或洛杉矶街头走一走
Dialogue: 1,0:11:17.12,0:11:19.44,Original,,0,0,0,,take a stroll in Tokyo or Los Angeles,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.84,0:11:23.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,你会明显感到霓虹灯已经过时了
Dialogue: 1,0:11:19.84,0:11:23.76,Original,,0,0,0,,and you'll get the distinct impression that neon is definitely passé.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.04,0:11:28.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,如今，电子招牌成为公共场所沟通交流的方式
Dialogue: 1,0:11:25.04,0:11:28.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Today, electronic signs are the way to communicate in public.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.92,0:11:34.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,那么，这些光彩夺目的未来奇迹究竟是如何制造的呢？
Dialogue: 1,0:11:29.92,0:11:34.64,Original,,0,0,0,,So, how are these futuristic miracles of light and colour actually made?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.68,0:11:43.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,数字电子招牌被用作巨型电视屏幕
Dialogue: 1,0:11:39.68,0:11:43.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Digital electronic signboards are used as giant television screens.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.48,0:11:48.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,有的只有几米高，而有的则庞大无比
Dialogue: 1,0:11:44.48,0:11:48.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Some are just a few metres tall, whilst others are simply massive.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.96,0:11:57.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,招牌的诞生始于电脑生成的设计方案，由工程师和建筑师制定
Dialogue: 1,0:11:50.96,0:11:57.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The creation of a sign starts with computer-generated plans drawn up by engineers and architects.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.04,0:12:07.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,数百万颗微小发光二极管
Dialogue: 1,0:12:03.04,0:12:07.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Millions of tiny lights, or light-emitting diodes called elements,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.44,0:12:08.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,构成了屏幕的表面
Dialogue: 1,0:12:07.44,0:12:08.64,Original,,0,0,0,,make up the screen's surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.92,0:12:16.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些灯珠由锗、氮化镓和硅半导体组成，外层覆以塑料
Dialogue: 1,0:12:09.92,0:12:16.16,Original,,0,0,0,,These elements are made up of germanium, gallium nitride, and silicon semiconductors, covered with plastic.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.44,0:12:20.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些灯珠需要要排列成点阵
Dialogue: 1,0:12:17.44,0:12:20.56,Original,,0,0,0,,These elements have to be placed so as to form a matrix.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.32,0:12:29.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,点亮一颗灯珠只需10到20毫安的电流，寿命约15万小时
Dialogue: 1,0:12:22.32,0:12:29.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Lighting up an element requires only 10 to 20 milliamps, and they last for about 150,000 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.32,0:12:38.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,所有导线都布置在点阵的背面
Dialogue: 1,0:12:36.32,0:12:38.88,Original,,0,0,0,,All the wires are placed at the back of the matrix.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.28,0:12:42.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,这样既隐藏了招牌背后的部件，又能使其免受风吹雨打
Dialogue: 1,0:12:39.28,0:12:42.72,Original,,0,0,0,,This conceals everything behind the sign and shelters it from the weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.16,0:12:47.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,根据人们观看招牌的距离
Dialogue: 1,0:12:44.16,0:12:47.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Depending upon the distance from which the sign will be seen, 
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.22,0:12:52.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,灯珠间距从2.5毫米到数厘米不等
Dialogue: 1,0:12:47.22,0:12:52.48,Original,,0,0,0,,spaces between the elements vary from 2.5 millimeters to several centimeters.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.44,0:12:56.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,电气连接使用的导线必须接得牢固
Dialogue: 1,0:12:53.44,0:12:56.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The electrical connections are made with wires firmly connected
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.64,0:12:59.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,以抵抗招牌移动时产生的震动
Dialogue: 1,0:12:56.64,0:12:59.84,Original,,0,0,0,,to resist shaking caused by movement of the signboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.20,0:13:07.38,Translation,,0,0,0,,各点阵必须协同工作
Dialogue: 1,0:13:05.20,0:13:07.38,Original,,0,0,0,,The matrices must operate together
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.38,0:13:11.22,Translation,,0,0,0,,需要控制器在彼此之间传递信息
Dialogue: 1,0:13:07.38,0:13:11.22,Original,,0,0,0,,and require controllers which send information from one to the other
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.22,0:13:13.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,以便每个模块组能控制自己的画面
Dialogue: 1,0:13:11.22,0:13:13.68,Original,,0,0,0,,so each group controls its own image.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.80,0:13:23.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,每个点阵都通过连接器， 独立接入5V 电源、
Dialogue: 1,0:13:16.80,0:13:23.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Each matrix has to be electronically powered and integrated to its own 5 volt element illuminating connector.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.64,0:13:31.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,有时点阵由两部分组成
Dialogue: 1,0:13:28.64,0:13:31.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Sometimes the matrices are made in two pieces,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.84,0:13:35.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,LED面板和控制电路
Dialogue: 1,0:13:31.84,0:13:35.12,Original,,0,0,0,,one supporting the elements and the other having the components.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.60,0:13:39.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,两张电路板连接起来就可以工作
Dialogue: 1,0:13:35.60,0:13:39.52,Original,,0,0,0,,In this case, it simply requires two cards to establish the contact.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.88,0:13:48.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在连接信号线
Dialogue: 1,0:13:46.88,0:13:48.72,Original,,0,0,0,,They now connect the information cable,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.96,0:13:51.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,用以点亮和熄灭灯珠
Dialogue: 1,0:13:48.96,0:13:51.20,Original,,0,0,0,,which lights up and extinguishes the elements.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.08,0:13:53.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,每个点阵有两个连接器
Dialogue: 1,0:13:52.08,0:13:53.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Each matrix has two connectors
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.96,0:13:58.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,一个供电， 另一个传输数据
Dialogue: 1,0:13:53.96,0:13:58.72,Original,,0,0,0,,one which supplies the electric current and the other which carries the sign's information.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.08,0:14:02.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,他们逐个检验每个点阵的工作情况
Dialogue: 1,0:14:00.08,0:14:02.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Here they verify the functioning of each matrix.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.32,0:14:08.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后就可以把各点阵拼接起来，组装成招牌
Dialogue: 1,0:14:04.32,0:14:08.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Then they can begin to join the matrices together to construct the sign board.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.92,0:14:12.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,各种颜色按屏幕显示的排列组合
Dialogue: 1,0:14:09.92,0:14:12.80,Original,,0,0,0,,All the colours are assembled as they will be seen on screen.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.56,0:14:16.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,点阵板可安装在室外
Dialogue: 1,0:14:14.56,0:14:16.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The boards can be exterior mounted,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.72,0:14:18.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,但容易受到天气影响
Dialogue: 1,0:14:16.72,0:14:18.00,Original,,0,0,0,,but are vulnerable to the weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.50,0:14:21.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,为应对这一点，会安装防水橡胶条
Dialogue: 1,0:14:18.50,0:14:21.60,Original,,0,0,0,,To counteract this, a waterproof rubber strip is fixed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.28,0:14:27.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,各点阵现在被拼装在一起
Dialogue: 1,0:14:25.28,0:14:27.28,Original,,0,0,0,,The matrices are now assembled together.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.60,0:14:32.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后每10个点阵拼接成一个模组
Dialogue: 1,0:14:29.60,0:14:32.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Then 10 matrices are joined to make up a module.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.40,0:14:43.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,此时插入信号线
Dialogue: 1,0:14:40.40,0:14:43.60,Original,,0,0,0,,At this stage, they insert the sign board conductor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.44,0:14:52.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后接上电源线
Dialogue: 1,0:14:51.44,0:14:52.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the wires are connected.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.36,0:14:57.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些导线传输电源和招牌的数据
Dialogue: 1,0:14:53.36,0:14:57.84,Original,,0,0,0,,These wires transmit electric current and all the information relating to the sign.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.48,0:15:04.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,LED只需约5伏的低压电流
Dialogue: 1,0:15:00.48,0:15:04.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The elements require a very low voltage current, about 5 volts.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.20,0:15:09.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,每个模组都配有各自的转换器以保持电压稳定
Dialogue: 1,0:15:05.20,0:15:09.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Each module is then provided with its own converter to maintain a steady voltage.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.04,0:15:16.34,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后所有模组被装进支架上
Dialogue: 1,0:15:13.04,0:15:16.34,Original,,0,0,0,,Then all the modules are assembled in the signboard support
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.34,0:15:20.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,并完成各模组之间众多电气连接
Dialogue: 1,0:15:16.34,0:15:20.64,Original,,0,0,0,,and the many electrical connections linking the different modules are made.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.52,0:15:31.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,这块巨型招牌由35个模组和12个点阵组成
Dialogue: 1,0:15:25.52,0:15:31.36,Original,,0,0,0,,This gigantic signboard is a composition of 35 modules and 12 matrices.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.00,0:15:37.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在它已接近完工
Dialogue: 1,0:15:36.00,0:15:37.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Now it's almost finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.84,0:15:42.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,屏幕的色调、对比度、亮度和分辨率都会逐一检查
Dialogue: 1,0:15:37.84,0:15:42.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The color hues, contrast, luminosity, and resolution of the screen are checked.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.04,0:15:56.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,这块招牌由12万颗LED组成，制造耗时近3个月
Dialogue: 1,0:15:49.04,0:15:56.64,Original,,0,0,0,,This signboard is made of 120,000 electrical light diodes, and takes nearly 3 months to manufacture.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.24,0:16:04.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,下次你漫步皮卡迪利广场时，你就会知道那些巨型屏幕背后藏着什么
Dialogue: 1,0:15:58.24,0:16:04.96,Original,,0,0,0,,So the next time you take a stroll down Piccadilly Circus, you'll know what goes on behind those giant screens.
Dialogue: 2,0:15:58.24,0:16:01.49,Annotation,,0,0,0,,皮卡迪利广场：伦敦著名地标
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.40,0:16:17.02,Translation,,0,0,0,,如果你不是那种早起， 悠闲享用早餐的人
Dialogue: 1,0:16:12.40,0:16:17.02,Original,,0,0,0,,If you aren't the type to rise at the crack of dawn and enjoy a leisurely breakfast
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.02,0:16:19.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,那么你可能吃的就是一碗麦片
Dialogue: 1,0:16:17.02,0:16:19.68,Original,,0,0,0,,the chances are you eat a bowl of cereal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.64,0:16:25.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,无论哪种方式，营养专家都认为早餐是一天中最重要的一餐
Dialogue: 1,0:16:20.64,0:16:25.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Either way, nutritional experts consider breakfast to be the most important meal of the day.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.40,0:16:30.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,所以倒好牛奶，随我们一起走进麦片工厂吧
Dialogue: 1,0:16:26.40,0:16:30.08,Original,,0,0,0,,So chill the milk and join us at the cereal factory.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.76,0:16:43.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,我们的早餐麦片诞生于美国基督复临安息日会的宗教信仰
Dialogue: 1,0:16:37.76,0:16:43.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Our breakfast cereals were born out of the religious beliefs of the American Seventh Day Adventists.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.76,0:16:43.70,Annotation,,0,0,0,,美国基督复临安息日会（亦称安息日会）。它起源于 19 世纪中叶美国的小型宗教运动，信徒将星期六定为安息日并进行礼拜
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.32,0:16:49.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,1860年，他们创办了一家疗养院，病人只吃麦片
Dialogue: 1,0:16:44.32,0:16:49.92,Original,,0,0,0,,In 1860, they founded a sanatorium where patients were fed only cereals.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.40,0:16:55.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,约翰·哈维·凯洛格医生发明的麦片，有印象吗？
Dialogue: 1,0:16:50.40,0:16:55.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Wheat flakes, invented by Doctor John Harvey Kellogg, ring any bells?
Dialogue: 2,0:16:50.40,0:16:54.40,Annotation,,0,0,0,,约翰·哈维·凯洛格：家乐氏创始人
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.16,0:17:00.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,他的兄弟威廉·基思建起第一座麦片工厂来销售产品
Dialogue: 1,0:16:56.16,0:17:00.48,Original,,0,0,0,,His brother William Keith built the first flakes factory to market the product,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.80,0:17:06.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一成功后来让超市货架上摆满琳琅满目的选择
Dialogue: 1,0:17:00.80,0:17:06.00,Original,,0,0,0,,whose success would later lead to the supermarket shelves heaving with choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.84,0:17:18.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎来到生产糖霜玉米片的工厂
Dialogue: 1,0:17:15.84,0:17:18.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome to the factory that makes frosted corn flakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.64,0:17:25.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先，至关重要的玉米粒要蒸煮2小时20分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:17:20.64,0:17:25.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Starting off, the all important corn kernels are cooked for 2 hours 20 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.84,0:17:30.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后玉米粒被这台螺旋输送器磨碎
Dialogue: 1,0:17:27.84,0:17:30.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the corn kernels are ground up by this worm screw,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.04,0:17:35.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,它也决定了配制麦片配方所需的量
Dialogue: 1,0:17:31.04,0:17:35.36,Original,,0,0,0,,which also determines the number of kilos needed to make up the cereal recipe.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.78,0:17:42.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,磨碎的玉米被送入干燥机
Dialogue: 1,0:17:39.78,0:17:42.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The ground corn is placed in a dryer unit,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.96,0:17:45.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是再次蒸煮前的重要步骤
Dialogue: 1,0:17:42.96,0:17:45.44,Original,,0,0,0,,an important step before they're cooked again.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.04,0:17:51.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,为了让玉米粒压成平整的片状，它们在压片辊中被压碎
Dialogue: 1,0:17:47.04,0:17:51.52,Original,,0,0,0,,To give them a nice flat shape, the corn kernels are crushed in the flake roller.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.36,0:17:55.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,两个辊筒相向转动
Dialogue: 1,0:17:53.36,0:17:55.28,Original,,0,0,0,,2 rollers turn opposite to each other,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.36,0:17:59.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,玉米粒落入两辊之间的狭小间隙
Dialogue: 1,0:17:55.36,0:17:59.84,Original,,0,0,0,,and the kernels fall into the constricted space between them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.64,0:18:05.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,传送带把麦片送走并运往烤箱
Dialogue: 1,0:18:00.64,0:18:05.20,Original,,0,0,0,,The conveyor spirits the flakes away and transports them to the oven.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.84,0:18:15.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,麦片被不断抖动，确保上色均匀
Dialogue: 1,0:18:09.84,0:18:15.20,Original,,0,0,0,,They're shaken to make sure they will be uniformly brown.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.86,0:18:18.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,麦片出炉时已烘烤得恰到好处
Dialogue: 1,0:18:15.86,0:18:18.08,Original,,0,0,0,,The flakes exit the oven well browned.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.64,0:18:25.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台振动传送带分拣麦片，只保留尺寸合格的麦片
Dialogue: 1,0:18:20.64,0:18:25.40,Original,,0,0,0,,This vibrating conveyor sorts the flakes and retains only the right sized ones
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.86,0:18:33.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着滚筒搅拌麦片并向其喷洒 230摄氏度滚烫的糖液
Dialogue: 1,0:18:25.86,0:18:33.04,Original,,0,0,0,,and a drum mixes the flakes and sprays them with a sweet solution at a scalding 230 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.14,0:18:45.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,糖液烘干后，耙子把糖霜麦片均匀摊铺在帆布上
Dialogue: 1,0:18:39.14,0:18:45.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The sweet solution is dried, and a rake uniformly spreads out the frosted flakes on the canvas.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.28,0:18:51.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来，添加至关重要的维生素
Dialogue: 1,0:18:49.28,0:18:51.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Next, they add the all-important vitamins.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.64,0:18:55.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,麦片被送入这台旋转滚筒
Dialogue: 1,0:18:52.64,0:18:55.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The cereals are placed into this rotating drum,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.44,0:18:58.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,维生素由一组喷嘴喷洒到麦片上
Dialogue: 1,0:18:55.44,0:18:58.80,Original,,0,0,0,,and the vitamins sprayed onto the flakes by a series of jets.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.64,0:19:05.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,早餐麦片至此完成，随后送往包装区
Dialogue: 1,0:19:01.64,0:19:05.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The breakfast cereal is now finished and heads towards the packaging side.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.28,0:19:09.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台包装机把麦片装入袋中
Dialogue: 1,0:19:07.28,0:19:09.20,Original,,0,0,0,,This packager fills the bags with cereal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.84,0:19:12.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,它每分钟可处理40到45袋
Dialogue: 1,0:19:09.84,0:19:12.96,Original,,0,0,0,,It can handle between 40 and 45 bags a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.60,0:19:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂不只生产麦片，还生产软麦片棒
Dialogue: 1,0:19:15.60,0:19:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,This plant doesn't only make cereals; it also makes soft cereal bars.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.96,0:19:25.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,揉合机把燕麦片、大米和糖浆等原料混合
Dialogue: 1,0:19:20.96,0:19:25.60,Original,,0,0,0,,This kneader mixes the ingredients: oat flakes, rice, and syrup.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.80,0:19:50.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,充分混合后，被倒一个大的容器中
Dialogue: 1,0:19:46.80,0:19:50.56,Original,,0,0,0,,When well mixed, the preparation is poured into a large container.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.84,0:19:54.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,料斗中的原料被倒上传送带
Dialogue: 1,0:19:51.84,0:19:54.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The contents of the bin are emptied onto a conveyor,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.76,0:19:57.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,并将混合物铺展开来
Dialogue: 1,0:19:55.76,0:19:57.92,Original,,0,0,0,,and the preparation is spread out.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.28,0:20:03.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,巧克力碎被加入混合物中
Dialogue: 1,0:20:01.28,0:20:03.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Chocolate chips are added to the preparation.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.40,0:20:12.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,混合物被压辊压成所需的棒状厚度
Dialogue: 1,0:20:08.40,0:20:12.28,Original,,0,0,0,,The mix is compressed to the desired bar thickness by a roller.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.30,0:20:21.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后分条机把混合物分成 35条等宽长条，裁切机再切成合适的长度
Dialogue: 1,0:20:14.30,0:20:21.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The bar separator then divides the mix into 35 equal strips, and a guillotine cuts the bars into their proper length.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.80,0:20:34.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,麦片棒排列整齐，为最后一步做准备
Dialogue: 1,0:20:31.80,0:20:34.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The bars are lined up, preparing them for the final step.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.60,0:20:47.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,麦片棒被转向，由并排改为前后排列
Dialogue: 1,0:20:43.60,0:20:47.84,Original,,0,0,0,,Side by side, the bars are turned so that they run one behind the other.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.72,0:20:55.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台滚筒把焦糖涂到麦片棒上，糖衣随后冷却定型
Dialogue: 1,0:20:50.72,0:20:55.12,Original,,0,0,0,,This roller slathers caramel onto the bars, which will eventually cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.44,0:21:00.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在到了生产的最后阶段：裹上巧克力
Dialogue: 1,0:20:57.44,0:21:00.96,Original,,0,0,0,,They're now at the final stage of production, coating with chocolate.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.92,0:21:05.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一批大约需要180公斤巧克力
Dialogue: 1,0:21:01.92,0:21:05.28,Original,,0,0,0,,About 180 kilos of chocolate are needed for this run.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.96,0:21:19.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在制作完成，麦片棒即可包装
Dialogue: 1,0:21:16.96,0:21:19.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Now finished, the bars are ready for packaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.14,0:21:35.82,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器把麦片棒逐根装袋，随后送到一群馋嘴的孩子手中
Dialogue: 1,0:21:30.14,0:21:35.82,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine individually bags the bars before being sent out to a gaggle of hungry children.
